  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1118 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nAn amplifying ridge aloft is forecast to prevail over the Plains,\ndownstream from troughing in the West. Above average temps and dry\nweather will be the rule into the weekend.\n\nChanges in the weather pattern occur by early next week. Energy in\nthe Southwest will move east toward the Plains, while a trough in\nthe northern stream dives down into the country from Canada. The\nlatter system will force a stronger cold front south into the\nregion Monday night into Tuesday. Models have some precip over the\nregion as the wave and front interact. Temps should drop to near\nor slightly below average behind this front.",
